        answer: "Most people see meaningful improvement within 4 to 6 weeks, and the majority recover within 3 months without surgery. Recovery is rarely linear. Leg symptoms often improve in stages, and some residual sensations can linger for several months even as function returns. The most useful signal I track is whether the pain is moving back up the leg toward the spine (centralizing), which tends to predict a faster recovery."
