        answer: "No. A herniated disc is the most common cause, but sciatic-type pain can also come from narrowing of the opening where the nerve leaves the spine (foraminal stenosis), the deep buttock muscles such as piriformis, sacroiliac joint irritation, or pain referred from the hip. Sorting out which structure is actually driving symptoms matters, because the plan changes significantly depending on the source."
