      primaryStrategy: "For the nerve type of thoracic outlet syndrome (neurogenic TOS) without significant weakness or muscle wasting, a monitored trial of rehabilitation is usually the first step, and change often takes 3 to 6 months. Significant or worsening weakness or wasting needs a prompt medical assessment, because it can change that order (the 2024 international INTOS consensus).",
      secondaryStrategy: "Spending less time in the positions that bring on symptoms, such as arms overhead or heavy carrying, can ease symptoms while the exercise program builds tolerance.",
      preventionStrategy: "Keeping up strength around the shoulders and shoulder blades, and breaking up long spells in the positions that bring on symptoms, may help symptoms stay settled.",
